discussion_comments.comment_body:
Updated to address the review feedback from @chatgpt-codex-connector — good catch on the CLI provider snapshot issue.

The fix moves extension resolution **before** `resolve_provider()`, so the extensions are now passed to `providers::create()`. This ensures CLI providers (`codex_acp`, `claude_code`) — which snapshot MCP servers at construction time via `extension_configs_to_mcp_servers()` — receive the correct extensions during delegation.

```rust
// build_task_config — extensions resolved FIRST, then provider created WITH them
let mut extensions = EnabledExtensionsState::extensions_or_default(...);
// merge recipe extensions
// apply filter
let provider = self.resolve_provider(params, recipe, session, &extensions).await?;
// resolve_provider now passes extensions to create() instead of Vec::new()
```

This also fixes a pre-existing issue: `resolve_provider` always passed `Vec::new()` to `providers::create()`, meaning CLI providers never received MCP servers during delegation — even for parent session extensions. The main session flow (`recreate_provider_for_session`) correctly passed extensions to `create()`, but the subagent delegation path did not.

| Provider type | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Standard (databricks, ollama, openai) | ✅ worked | ✅ works |
| CLI/ACP (codex_acp, claude_code) | ❌ no MCP servers | ✅ correct MCP servers |

